      "lineNbr": 2916,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-25T00:20:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Can deep sleep happen between TPM2_Startup and TPM2_Shutdown?\n\nno, deep sleep is only allowed in the situations when there is firmware that calls TPM2_Startup(STATE) on the resume path. so, if Shutdown(STATE) was not called on suspend it would fail anyway. on request from DRM, we do have custom logic that preserves orderly counters regardless: even if there was no Shutdown(STATE), but it was only a sudden AP reboot, we still have the actual values and we keep them instead of rounding up. \nbut that\u0027s only for sudden AP reboots when GSC keeps running. if there\u0027s, for example, a sudden power loss for the entire device including GSC we\u0027d still lose the orderly spaces, of course.",
      "parentUuid": "f7e43472_78659ba8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2916,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 2916,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "46de1ae22c8117642d97ff1dd1a6bb1114cdf8c4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
